 "description": "# \n\nTask Description: Problem Statement Given is a number sequence A of length N.\nFind the number of integers i <=ft(1 <= i <= N\\right) with the following property:\n\nFor every integer j <=ft(1 <= j <= N\\right) such that i \\neq j , A_j does not divide A_i.\nTask Constraint: All values in input are integers.\n1 <= N <= 2 * 10^5\n1 <= A_i <= 10^6\nTask Input: Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 A_2 \\cdots A_N\nTask Output: Print the answer.\nTask Samples: input: 5\n24 11 8 3 16 output: 3\n\nThe integers with the property are 2,3, and 4.\ninput: 4\n5 5 5 5 output: 0\n\nNote that there can be multiple equal numbers.\ninput: 10\n33 18 45 28 8 19 89 86 2 4 output: 5\n\n## Constraints\nAll values in input are integers.\n1 <= N <= 2 * 10^5\n1 <= A_i <= 10^6\n\n## Input\nInput is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 A_2 \\cdots A_N\n\n## Output\nPrint the answer.\n\n## Examples\n['input: 5\\n24 11 8 3 16 output: 3\\n\\nThe integers with the property are 2,3, and 4.', 'input: 4\\n5 5 5 5 output: 0\\n\\nNote that there can be multiple equal numbers.', 'input: 10\\n33 18 45 28 8 19 89 86 2 4 output: 5']",
